<title>PAKISTAN: Pakistan gold rates seen easing on lower demand.</title>
<headline>Pakistan gold rates seen easing on lower demand.</headline>
<dateline>KARACHI, Pakistan 1997-02-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>Pakistan gold rates are likely to ease on higher supplies and lower demand for jewellery when trading resumes on Wednesday after the Moslem Eid al-Fitr holiday, dealers said.</p>
<p>Silver rates, unchanged last week, were likely to remain steady, one dealer said.</p>
<p>    Gold 24 carat in rupees per 10 grammes SUNDAY   Feb 2</p>
<p>							 4,718    4,787</p>
<p>    Silver per 1,000 grammes		   7,715    7,715</p>
<p>($1 = 40.22 rupees)</p>
<p>-- Ibrahim Khan 9221-5685192</p>
</text>
